course: dictionary
lesson: 6170
title: The smallest allowed: minimum
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Minimum means the smallest amount, number or level that is possible or allowed. «The minimum age for this ride is 12» means nobody younger than 12 may go on it. The rule sets the lowest limit.
explain: Minimum can be a noun or an adjective. As a noun, it is the smallest value itself: «The minimum is 1.6 millimetres.» As an adjective, it describes a noun: «the minimum age», «the minimum height». Look at the words around it to see which one it is.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «The minimum wage is the lowest pay per hour allowed by law.» If you swap in "the smallest pay allowed by law" and it still makes sense, you have the right meaning.
explain: Some useful phrases: «at a minimum» means at least, «keep to a minimum» means make something as small as you can, and «the bare minimum» means only just enough.
fact: Minimum means the smallest amount, number or level that is possible or allowed.
fact: «The minimum wage is the lowest pay per hour allowed by law.»
fact: In maths, the minimum is the lowest value in a set of numbers.
fact: «At a minimum» means at least.
fact: Paying only the minimum can keep a debt going for years, so the smallest amount is not always the best choice.
exercise: «The minimum age for this ride is 12.» What does minimum mean here? | The biggest age allowed | *The smallest age allowed | The age of the oldest rider | The number of riders
exercise: Find the minimum in the numbers 7, 3, 9, 5. Which number is it? | 5 | 7 | *3 | 9
exercise: «Keep your screen time to a minimum.» What does this mean? | Use it as much as you can | *Make it as small as you can | Use it only at night | Put it in a box
test: «The minimum wage is the lowest pay per hour allowed by law.» What is the lowest pay allowed by law called? | Average wage | Maximum wage | *Minimum wage | Extra wage
test: Dad says, «Just do the bare minimum tonight.» What does the bare minimum mean? | *Only just enough, the least needed | A bare, empty room | The most you can do | The middle amount
exam: Mia's teacher says, «You need a minimum of 5 correct spellings.» What does minimum mean? | The most spellings allowed | *The least number needed, at least 5 | Five times the spellings | Only the first spelling
